{
  "title": "Me lo {imv:dia}, per favore: glielo {ip:spiego} io",
  "translation": "Give it to me, please: I'll explain it to him",
  "topics": "Combined pronouns, the formal imperative",
  "grammar": {
    "explain": [
      {
        "h": "Two pronouns together"
      },
      "When a verb has an indirect and a direct pronoun, the indirect one comes first. It changes slightly: its *-i* becomes *-e*, and *gli* or *le* both become *glie-*, written as one word with the next pronoun.",
      {
        "table": {
          "head": [
            "Indirect",
            "+ lo",
            "+ la",
            "+ li",
            "+ le",
            "+ ne"
          ],
          "rows": [
            [
              "mi",
              "m**e** lo",
              "m**e** la",
              "m**e** li",
              "m**e** le",
              "m**e** ne"
            ],
            [
              "ti",
              "t**e** lo",
              "t**e** la",
              "t**e** li",
              "t**e** le",
              "t**e** ne"
            ],
            [
              "gli / le",
              "**glie**lo",
              "**glie**la",
              "**glie**li",
              "**glie**le",
              "**glie**ne"
            ],
            [
              "ci",
              "c**e** lo",
              "c**e** la",
              "c**e** li",
              "c**e** le",
              "c**e** ne"
            ],
            [
              "vi",
              "v**e** lo",
              "v**e** la",
              "v**e** li",
              "v**e** le",
              "v**e** ne"
            ]
          ]
        }
      },
      "Since *glielo* covers both *to him* and *to her*, only the context tells you which one is meant.",
      {
        "table": {
          "head": [
            "Sentence",
            "With pronouns"
          ],
          "rows": [
            [
              "Ti {ip:dico} il segreto.",
              "Te lo {ip:dico}."
            ],
            [
              "{ip:Do} il libro a Marco.",
              "Glielo {ip:do}."
            ],
            [
              "{ip:Do} la lettera ad Anna.",
              "Gliela {ip:do}."
            ],
            [
              "Ci {imv:porti} due caffè.",
              "Ce ne {imv:porti} due."
            ]
          ]
        }
      },
      {
        "h": "Where they go"
      },
      "They follow the same rules as single pronouns. They stand before a conjugated verb and attach to an infinitive: *Te lo {ip:voglio} dire* or *{ip:Voglio} dirtelo*. In the [pp:passato prossimo] the participle agrees with *lo, la, li, le*: *Te l'{pp:ho dett**o**}. Gliel'{pp:ho dat**a**}.*",
      {
        "h": "The formal imperative"
      },
      "To address someone as *Lei*, the endings swap, as in the *congiuntivo*: *-are* verbs take *-i*, and *-ere* and *-ire* verbs take *-a*.",
      {
        "table": {
          "head": [
            "Infinitive",
            "tu",
            "Lei"
          ],
          "rows": [
            [
              "parlare",
              "{imv:parl**a**}!",
              "{imv:parl**i**}!"
            ],
            [
              "prendere",
              "{imv:prend**i**}!",
              "{imv:prend**a**}!"
            ],
            [
              "sentire",
              "{imv:sent**i**}!",
              "{imv:sent**a**}!"
            ],
            [
              "finire",
              "{imv:fin**isci**}!",
              "{imv:fin**isca**}!"
            ]
          ]
        }
      },
      "Irregular forms come from the *io* form of the present: *{ip:vengo} → {csp:venga}, {ip:faccio} → {csp:faccia}, {ip:dico} → {csp:dica}, {ip:vado} → {csp:vada}, {ip:esco} → {csp:esca}*. Also *essere → {csp:sia}*, *avere → {csp:abbia}*, *dare → {csp:dia}*, *stare → {csp:stia}*.",
      {
        "h": "Pronouns in commands"
      },
      "With *Lei*, pronouns always come before the verb. With *tu*, they are attached to it.",
      {
        "table": {
          "head": [
            "tu",
            "Lei"
          ],
          "rows": [
            [
              "{imv:Dimmi}!",
              "Mi {imv:dica}!"
            ],
            [
              "{imv:Dammelo}!",
              "Me lo {imv:dia}!"
            ],
            [
              "{imv:Alzati}!",
              "Si {imv:alzi}!"
            ]
          ]
        }
      }
    ]
  },
  "use": {
    "exercises": [
      {
        "type": "gap",
        "prompt": "Replace the words with combined pronouns.",
        "questions": [
          "Ti {ip:dico} il segreto. → [[Te lo]] {ip:dico}.",
          "Mi {ip:dai} le chiavi? → [[Me le]] {ip:dai}?",
          "{ip:Do} il libro a Marco. → [[Glielo]] {ip:do}.",
          "{ip:Spiego} la regola ad Anna. → [[Gliela]] {ip:spiego}.",
          "Vi {ip:mando} i documenti. → [[Ve li]] {ip:mando}.",
          "Ci {ip:porta} due caffè. → [[Ce ne]] {ip:porta} due."
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "gap",
